// vocabulary.js — THE VOCABULARY, meaning → form → shape as one table (lane F5-BC; A4 whole; RULINGS §1(c), C-28, C-29;
// A3 §5.6 for the ceremony ids; A5 §8 for the sheets). Owns: the row type (A4 §6.1 plus `ceremonyIn ceremonyOut sound
// degraded camera label chip strip`), the house tokens, the seven hues and six neutrals with their measured contrast, the
// rhythm classes, the mass unit (`m = bytes ÷ 5,154,939,136`, `mT`, `mR`; RULINGS §3 C-37), the file bytes and layer counts
// of the minds (A5 §2.0, measured 2026-10-30), the 148 ceremony ids of A3 §5.6 and A5's seven, the label words kept from
// floorModel.js, the ceremony matcher every `transitions()` uses, and the rows: A4's 166 (V-001 … V-200) plus the eighteen
// the review §5c names (V-201 … V-218; its "twelve" lists thirteen states, its "four more" lists five sheets). Every row
// names its record kinds; `test/vocabulary.test.mjs` fails the build on the fourteen predicates of A4 §6.2. Refuses: a row
// with no record (law 1), a raw hex outside `HUES`, a click target outside A9's tabs, green on any actor but the foreman (the
// seal and his droplets name him as sender). Implements: A4 §2–§7; master §2.3, §3.9. Invariants (design §18): "every pixel
// has a provenance chain" (assay → kind → row → law test). Faults (§16): none. Size: this module is the table itself (A4
// §1: "the table is the design"), one row per state of every kind, so it runs past 500 lines by design and is split by
// section headers, never by file; its budget is 1,200 lines.

